{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He shall not defile himself, a husband among his people.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: the husband shall not defile himself to a disqualified wife, for through her he profanes his priesthood." "<b>And the Ramban,</b> of blessed memory, explained: 'a husband' (בעל) means a nobleman, as in (II Samuel 6:2) בעלי יהודה — the nobles of Judah. He said: a nobleman shall not defile himself among his people — so as to diminish his honor; for because of the priest's rank, since he is fit to be the great and noble one among his people, Scripture cautions him not to profane his rank through the impurity of the dead. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted 'among his people' (בעמיו) as referring to a corpse that is within his people — this excludes a met mitzvah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:31.463656445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}